trans-unit.note:
@deatherit Alternative copy of the string in ../Settings/AchievementSettingsWidget.cpp:216 , which does contain variables for each element.
"Login token generated at" would be usually followed by the date and time when the user has logged into RetroAchivements, but in this case, there's no variable.
Please copy the contents of the aforementioned string, but removing the variables.

@abagyr900 For Crowdin, it means:
one → when a number ends with 1, except 11 (1, 21, 31…) few → when a number ends with 2, 3, or 4, except 12, 13, 14 (2, 3, 4, 22, 23, 24…) many → any other case (0, 5 to 20, 25 to 30, 35 to 40…)
Keep this in mind when doing translations.

@abagyr900 For Crowdin, it means:
